Hello {!Contact.FirstName},

Thank you for contacting Arizona State University. Reserve Officer Training Corps is a program that prepares you for a potential career in the United States military as a commissioned officer, all while earning your college degree.

ASU is one of the few universities in the nation that offers Army, Air Force and Navy ROTC units (Marine options are assigned to Navy ROTC). This program falls under the College of Liberal Arts and Sciences.

In ROTC, you’ll make the most of your college experience. You’ll hone your time-management skills, analytical skills and physical fitness. You will be required to take specific military classes, which will include physical training and leadership laboratory, where you will develop your leadership and teamwork abilities.

As a cadet or midshipman, there are many opportunities for scholarships and various training programs that the average college student would never have. Once you complete all mandatory training requirements and complete your bachelor’s degree, you will become a second lieutenant or ensign in your respective branch of service.

The links below will provide more information about the ASU ROTC unit and respective branches of service.

ASU Air Force ROTC (https://afrotc.clas.asu.edu/?home)
ASU Army ROTC (https://militaryscience.clas.asu.edu/)
ASU Navy ROTC (https://nrotc.asu.edu/)

{!User.Recruiter_Full_Name__c}
